    "body": "## Problem\n\nWith concealed text and `noinsert` or `noselect` in `completeopt`, the completion popup can appear too far left. Drawing has already adjusted the cached cursor column for conceal, but popup placement subtracts the concealed width again.\n\nFound while testing neovim/neovim#40897, but also reproduced on upstream master without that PR.\n\n## Solution\n\nRecompute the cursor column before applying the popup's conceal offset. This reuses the existing validation logic without adding state or changing conceal rendering.\n\nAdd a regression in the existing popupmenu tests covering normal, `noinsert`, and `noselect` completion.",
